    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "In `checkIfIsAvailable`, the new `dateOverrideExist` path uses `dayjs(date.start).add(utcOffset, \"minutes\") === dayjs(date.end).add(utcOffset, \"minutes\")` inside the `dateOverrides.find(...)` branch. That compares two Dayjs object identities, not their timestamps, so the exact-match branch only works if both sides are the same object reference. For ordinary overrides where `start !== end`, the branch will not recognize a zero-length or exact-time override as intended and the function can fall through to the working-hours/busy checks instead of honoring the override semantics. Also observed in: packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/slots.ts",
